       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose:\n\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day. The usual split is 850 mg three times daily with meals.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000 mg/day, or 2,500 mg/day for some formulations.\n\nNormal kidney and liver function doesn't change that ceiling. A dose this high also raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe intended dose may have been a typo. Possible corrections:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, such as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO twice daily**, which is a typical dose for starting or titrating\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do need a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber of record. I can't enter it from here."
      }
