       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming that the dose is intentional doesn't change the answer. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and the order would be 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin (2,550 mg/day).\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled maximum.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can enter that now.\n- **Use the pharmacy or prescriber pathway.** If you believe this patient needs a supratherapeutic dose, pharmacy review or the attending's direct override should handle it. They can document the rationale and monitoring plan, such as lactate and renal function.\n- **Check the indication with endocrinology or pharmacy.** If the goal is stronger glycemic control, adding or switching to another agent is usually safer than going past the metformin ceiling.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter one of the in-range doses."
      }
